  "id": "animal-physiology",
  "title": "How Animals Work: Comparative Physiology",
  "summary": "An audio-first comparative investigation of how animals maintain their internal conditions and coordinate movement: regulation, gas exchange, circulation, water and salt balance, digestion, molecular muscle force, biomechanics, electrical nerve signaling and synapses. Further physiology chapters can cover sensing, temperature, hormones, defense and reproduction. The course compares many animal lineages instead of treating humans as an anatomical default.",
